# THE CENTROID — Prologue
# Opening scene (Day 4) followed by the flashbacks P01–P06.
# Format help: see scripts/story/story_parser.gd
# Manga direction: @page starts a page; @panel shape | cast (left to right) | what the panel shows.

@music main_theme
@title THE CENTROID
@card DAY 4 OF DARKNESS | Abandoned training ground | Continuous night
@bg training_ground

@page
@panel strip | - | Extreme wide establishing shot of an abandoned stone training courtyard at night under a black starless sky, broken wooden practice swords scattered across cracked flagstones, tall stone pillars, total darkness except a faint warm lantern glow at the far entrance, cold blue moonless shadows
> Darkness. Four days without the sun.
> An abandoned training ground stands silent. Broken wooden practice swords lie scattered across the ground.
@panel tall | kael | Low-angle shot of Kael walking between stone pillars holding up a small glowing lantern, his face lit warm from below, wary determined eyes, deep night shadows around him
> Footsteps echo between the stone pillars. Kael enters carrying a small lantern.
@panel wide | rhex | Medium-wide shot of a muscular figure sitting relaxed on worn stone steps in deep shadow, the lantern light just reaching his boots and his smirking mouth, the silhouette of a spiky red mohawk
> Someone is sitting on the steps ahead.
@show right rhex
RHEX [smile]: I thought you'd never come.

@page
@panel square | kael | Close-up of Kael's face frozen in shock, eyes wide, lantern light flickering across his cheek, a bead of sweat
> Kael stops.
@show left kael
KAEL [shocked]: Rhex...
@panel wide | kael, rhex | Medium two-shot across the dark courtyard: Kael on the left holding the lantern, Rhex on the right rising from the steps and turning toward him, long shadows stretching between them
> Rhex stands and slowly turns toward him.
RHEX: How long has it been? Since we last trained here?
KAEL [angry]: Before you betrayed us.
@panel square | rhex | Close-up of Rhex's mocking half smile, the scar across his cheek, red eyes glinting in the lantern light
> Rhex smiles.
RHEX [smile]: You still talk like a child.

@page
@panel action | kael | Kael shouting in fury, leaning forward, the lantern swinging wildly, dramatic speed lines behind him, intense close-medium shot
KAEL [angry]: You helped kill Seran. You helped steal the Centroid. And now the whole world is suffering.
@panel wide | rhex, kael | Over-the-shoulder shot from behind Kael: Rhex looking down at him with cold contempt, arms crossed, towering and broad
RHEX [determined]: Still blaming everyone else because you're too weak to change anything?
@panel square | kael | Extreme close-up of Kael's hand tightening around the wrapped grip of his sword at his hip, knuckles white
> Kael grips his sword.
KAEL [determined]: Where are the others?

@page
@panel wide | rhex | Rhex turning away, gesturing at the ruined courtyard with its broken training posts and scattered practice swords, nostalgic yet bitter
RHEX: You haven't seen your old friends in months, and that's the first thing you ask?
> Rhex looks around the ruined training ground.
RHEX: Remember this place? We used to fight until Auren ordered us to stop.
@panel strip | kael | Kael standing in the empty dark courtyard looking into the distance, faint translucent ghostly images of young fighters sparring with wooden swords appear over the ruins like a memory
> Kael looks toward the empty courtyard. The sound of wooden swords echoes faintly.
@fx CLACK | swing_light
> And the memory comes back.
@hide all

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- P01
@flashback on
@music story_calm
@card YEARS EARLIER | Before the darkness | The organization's headquarters
@bg hq_night

@page
@panel wide | auren | Peaceful night: the elderly Auren standing alone on the stone terrace outside a mountain fortress headquarters, gazing up at a sky full of brilliant stars, warm lantern light behind him
> Auren stands outside the headquarters, watching the stars.
> Seran approaches with two cups of tea.
@panel wide | seran, auren | Seran handing Auren a steaming cup of tea on the terrace, both men in a friendly moment, warm lantern light, starry sky
@show left seran
SERAN: You haven't slept.
@show right auren
AUREN: Neither have you.
SERAN: Someone has to make sure you don't wander into the mountains again.
> Auren takes the cup.
@panel square | auren, seran | Close two-shot of Auren sipping tea and Seran smirking beside him, relaxed banter between old friends
AUREN: Where's Veyr?
SERAN: Reading. Again.
AUREN: He should sleep occasionally.
SERAN: You could tell him that.

@page
@panel splash | - | Spectacular wide night sky over a dark forest and distant mountains: a brilliant burning meteor streaks across the stars, trailing white-gold fire, lighting the clouds
> Suddenly, a brilliant light crosses the sky.
@fx FWOOOM | fire_burst
> The earth shakes. A burning object falls beyond the forest.
@fx KRA-KOOM | hit_heavy

@page
@panel wide | seran, auren | Seran and Auren on the terrace turning sharply toward a distant orange glow rising beyond the forest, tea spilling from a cup, faces lit by the far-off fire
> Both men turn toward the impact.
SERAN: What was that?
@panel square | auren | Close-up of Auren calmly setting down his tea cup, eyes fixed on the glowing horizon, serious and resolute
> Auren puts down his tea.
AUREN: I don't know.
SERAN: You're going to find out, aren't you?
AUREN: Wake Veyr.
@hide all

@bg crater
@page
@panel strip | veyr, auren, seran | Three figures standing at the rim of a huge smoking impact crater at night, melted glowing earth, steam rising, and at its center a small black stone with a faint line of light
> The three leaders reach the impact crater.
@panel square | - | Close-up of a perfectly smooth black stone resting in melted glassy earth, untouched by fire, a thin glowing line of white light running through its center
> At its center lies a black, perfectly smooth stone, surrounded by melted earth.
> Unlike the surrounding rocks, it is untouched by the fire. A faint line of light runs through its center.
@panel wide | veyr, seran | Veyr crouching close to the black stone at the crater's center, examining it with intense fascination; Seran standing behind him, arms crossed, wary
> Veyr examines it closely.
@show left veyr
VEYR: It came through the sky, struck the ground, and didn't break.
@show right seran
SERAN: Then leave it here.
VEYR: Aren't you curious?
SERAN: About something that just fell out of the heavens? Not particularly.

@page
@panel tall | auren | Auren kneeling beside the black stone, his open hand slowly approaching it, the glowing line on the stone brightening in response and lighting his face
> Auren kneels beside the stone. As his hand approaches it, the glowing line brightens.
> He withdraws his hand. The light fades.
@show right auren
AUREN: It responds to us.
@panel wide | veyr, auren | Veyr reaching out to touch the stone, which stays dark and still; he glances at Auren with fascination and a hint of envy
VEYR: To you, perhaps.
> Veyr reaches for the stone. It remains still.
> He looks at Auren, fascinated.
VEYR: Try again.
@panel splash | auren, seran | Auren touching the black stone as the stars overhead visibly dim across the whole sky; Seran looking up at the darkening heavens in alarm, eerie silence
> Auren touches it. For a fraction of a second, the stars overhead seem to dim.
> Seran looks up.
SERAN: Did you see that?
> Auren stares at the stone.
AUREN: Yes.
> They carry it back to the headquarters for study.
@hide all

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- P02
@card SEVERAL WEEKS LATER | The organization's research chamber
@bg research_chamber

@page
@panel wide | auren, veyr, seran | A cluttered stone research chamber with scrolls, books and instruments; the black stone on a table beside glowing green Asterite crystals; Auren, Veyr and Seran studying it by daylight from a tall window
> The three leaders have spent weeks studying the mysterious stone.
> Auren has discovered that it reacts to a rare green mineral found in the surrounding mountains. Veyr calls the mineral Asterite.
@panel square | - | Close-up of the black stone beside a glowing green Asterite crystal, its line of light splitting into two distinct patterns, one radiant bright and one deep dark
> When the stone is placed near Asterite, the glowing line on its surface divides into two distinct patterns. One bright. One dark.
@panel wide | veyr, seran | Veyr proudly presenting a small carved pedestal of glowing green Asterite with the stone on it, explaining eagerly; Seran skeptical beside him
> Veyr has constructed a small pedestal from the mineral.
@show left veyr
VEYR: Look at the markings. Two configurations. The stone isn't producing light. It's controlling something.
@show right seran
SERAN: Controlling what?

@page
@panel wide | auren | Auren opening a wooden window shutter, bright daylight flooding the chamber and falling on the stone resting bright side up on the green pedestal
> Auren opens a shutter to the daylight outside.
> He places the stone on the pedestal, bright side facing upward. Nothing unusual happens.
@panel square | veyr | Close-up of Veyr's fingers carefully rotating the black stone on the green pedestal so its dark marking faces down, his eyes reflected in its surface
> Veyr rotates it so the dark mark aligns with the pedestal.
@bg research_dark
@panel splash | auren, veyr, seran | Exactly three men in the research chamber as it suddenly plunges into darkness: through the window the daylight drains away into an unnatural black sky; Auren, Veyr and Seran startled, lit only by the faint glow of the black stone on the green pedestal
> The chamber suddenly darkens. Outside, the daylight begins to vanish.
@fx VMMMMN | gravity
> Auren immediately turns the stone back.

@bg research_chamber
@page
@panel wide | seran, veyr | Daylight back in the chamber; Seran and Veyr standing motionless and stunned, dust drifting in the sunbeams
> The light returns. The three men stand motionless.
SERAN: What have we just done?
VEYR: We blocked the sunlight.
SERAN: That's impossible.
VEYR: You saw it.
@panel square | auren | Auren at the window looking up at the restored sun, grave and thoughtful
> Auren looks toward the sky.
@show right auren
AUREN: We didn't change the sun itself. We changed whether its light could reach us.
@panel wide | veyr, seran | Veyr with eyes shining with ambition, hand raised toward the stone; Seran grim beside him
> Veyr looks excited.
VEYR: Think about what this means. We could control the greatest force above this world.
@show right seran
SERAN: Or destroy everything beneath it.
@panel square | auren | Auren firmly taking the black stone from the pedestal into his hand, decisive
> Auren takes the stone from the pedestal.
@show right auren
AUREN: No one is using this again until we understand it.
@hide all

@page
@panel splash | - | A grand secured underground chamber with guards and torches: the Solar Altar, a large ring-stepped structure of stone and glowing green Asterite, with the black stone resting on top radiating a soft light
> Later, the organization constructs a larger Asterite structure — the Solar Altar — in a secured chamber, so they can investigate how to reverse or contain the stone's effects.
> Auren names the object the Centroid, because it acts as the central point of a force he cannot yet explain.
> The three leaders establish three rules: the stone must remain guarded; no member may activate it alone; and the dark configuration must never be used except to prevent a greater catastrophe.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- P03
@card MONTHS LATER | Headquarters balcony | Sunset
@bg balcony_sunset

@page
@panel strip | auren, seran | A fortress balcony at golden sunset, Auren and Seran leaning on the stone railing, overlooking a training yard far below
> Auren and Seran watch the organization's younger members training.
@panel wide | kael, thane | In the training yard at sunset: a younger teenage Kael sparring fiercely with wooden swords against his older brother Thane, dust flying; two other youths arguing in the background
> Kael is sparring with Thane. Iren and Zerin are arguing nearby.
@panel tall | veyr | Veyr alone at a desk inside by lamplight, absorbed in diagrams and drawings of the black stone
> Veyr is at a desk, studying the stone's diagrams.

@page
@panel wide | auren, seran | Two-shot on the sunset balcony: Auren smiling fondly, Seran with a wry expression
@show left auren
AUREN: They're getting stronger.
@show right seran
SERAN: Iren and Zerin nearly destroyed the training floor yesterday.
AUREN: Then they're enthusiastic.
SERAN: That's one word for it.
> Auren smiles.
@panel square | auren | Close-up of Auren turning to Seran with a thoughtful, searching look, the sunset behind him
AUREN: What do you think of Veyr?
> Seran looks surprised.
@panel wide | seran | Seran gazing out at the setting sun, serious, choosing his words
SERAN: He's brilliant. Nobody understands the Centroid better than him.
AUREN: That's not what I asked.
> Seran pauses.
SERAN: He thinks too much about what we could control and too little about what we should.
@panel square | auren, seran | Two different men side by side at the balcony railing seen from behind against the last light of the sunset: white-bearded Auren in pale robes and Seran in his dark grey coat, quiet and heavy
AUREN: And you?
SERAN: I think we should have left that thing in the crater.
> Auren looks back toward the training ground.
AUREN: Perhaps.
@hide all

@bg research_dark
@page
@panel wide | auren, veyr | Night: Auren standing in the doorway of a dark study lit by the eerie glow of the black stone; Veyr hunched over his notes at the desk
> Later that night, Auren visits Veyr.
@show left auren
AUREN: You're still studying?
@show right veyr
VEYR: I found another pattern. I believe the Centroid can connect us to whatever sent it here.
AUREN: Then stop.
@panel square | veyr | Close-up of Veyr's intense face, the stone's glow reflected in his cold violet eyes
VEYR: You don't even want to know what's out there?
AUREN: I want to know enough to protect our people.
VEYR: We could become strong enough that nobody would ever threaten us again.
@panel wide | auren, veyr | Auren placing a gentle hand on Veyr's shoulder, fatherly, while Veyr stares at the stone
AUREN: There's always someone stronger, Veyr.
VEYR: Then we should become stronger than them.
> Auren puts a hand on his shoulder.
AUREN: One day you'll understand that strength isn't the same as authority.
@panel tall | veyr | Veyr looking away into darkness, half of his face in shadow, a quiet resentment
> Veyr looks away.
> This is the last peaceful conversation between them.
@hide all

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- P04
@card LATER THAT YEAR | Forbidden research chamber
@bg forbidden_chamber

@page
@panel wide | veyr | Veyr alone in a forbidden underground chamber, the black stone emitting swirling dark violet patterns and an eerie light, papers floating
> Veyr has secretly continued his research.
> The Centroid begins emitting a strange sound. A dark pattern appears on the stone, followed by a voice in Veyr's mind.
@fx WHMMMM | curse
THE VOICE: You understand what your leader fears.
@panel square | veyr | Veyr spinning around sharply, wary, searching the shadows, cold sweat
> Veyr turns around.
@show left veyr
VEYR: Who's there?
THE VOICE: He discovered the door. You understand how to open it.
@panel splash | veyr | Veyr standing small before the glowing dark stone while an immense shadowy cosmic presence with countless star-like eyes looms in the darkness above him, filling the chamber
VEYR: What do you want?
THE VOICE: Thirty-seven days without sunlight. Give us the darkness, and we will give you the power to command this world.
VEYR: Why me?
THE VOICE: Because you are willing to become what he refuses to be.
> Veyr hesitates.
VEYR: And the others?
THE VOICE: Those who follow you will share your strength.
@hide all

@page
@panel strip | veyr | Candlelit secret meeting: Veyr speaking persuasively to seven hooded figures in shadow around a table, faces hidden, conspiratorial
> Over the following weeks, he secretly persuades seven members to join him.
> He presents it as a way to end injustice permanently. He hides the space beings' true intentions, claiming the promised powers will allow the organization to impose peace.
> Not all seven join for the same reason. Some desire power, some believe Veyr's arguments, and others fear being left behind.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- P05
@music main_theme
@card THE FIRST BETRAYAL | Centroid chamber
@bg centroid_chamber

@page
@panel wide | auren, veyr | The Centroid chamber: Auren striding in to confront Veyr, who stands before the darkly glowing Centroid on its altar
> Auren discovers Veyr communicating with the unknown intelligence.
> He summons Seran and confronts Veyr.
@show left auren
AUREN: Tell me you haven't promised them the Centroid.
@show right veyr
VEYR: You saw what it can do. You know what we could become.
@panel square | auren | Close-up of Auren's grave face, disappointment in his eyes
AUREN: What did they ask for?
VEYR: Thirty-seven days of darkness.
@panel wide | seran, veyr | Seran stepping forward angrily toward Veyr, hand near his sword
> Seran takes a step forward.
@show left seran
SERAN: And you agreed?
VEYR: When it's over, nothing will threaten this world again.

@page
@panel wide | auren, veyr | Auren and Veyr face to face before the Centroid, intense standoff, the stone's glow between them
@show left auren
AUREN: Nothing will be allowed to oppose you. That's what they promised.
VEYR: You've spent your entire life stopping injustice one fight at a time. How many more people have to suffer before you admit it isn't enough?
AUREN: Peace that depends on fear is another kind of injustice.
@panel action | veyr | Veyr drawing his long blade in one swift flash of steel, speed lines, cold eyes
> Veyr draws his blade.
@fx SHING | swing_light
@show left seran
SERAN: Put that away.
VEYR: Stand aside.
@panel square | auren | Close-up of Auren, sorrow and love in his eyes, unafraid
@show left auren
AUREN: Veyr... I trusted you with the Centroid because I believed you would see beyond its power.
@panel square | veyr | Close-up of Veyr's face hardening into cold resolve, violet eyes narrowing
> Veyr's expression hardens.
VEYR: Then you trusted the wrong man.

@page
@panel action | veyr, auren | Veyr lunging with his long blade at the white-bearded Auren, who blocks the strike with his forearm, sparks flying, dynamic clash, only these two men
> He strikes.
@fx CLANG | block
> Auren blocks the first attack but refuses to deliver a killing blow.
@panel splash | auren | Tragic dramatic scene: the white-bearded Auren in pale robes staggering backward and falling, his robes swirling, struck by a blade thrust from a black-gloved hand that enters from the edge of the frame (the attacker is not shown), the dark glow of the stone on its altar behind him, no gore, heavy shadows
> Veyr uses that hesitation to stab him.
@fx SHK | hit_heavy
@hide left
> Auren falls.
@panel tall | kael | A younger Kael frozen in the chamber doorway, horror-struck, eyes wide and shining with tears
> Kael, arriving after hearing the commotion, sees his founder lying on the ground.
@show left kael
KAEL [shocked]: Auren!
@hide all

@page
@panel action | seran, veyr | Seran and Veyr clashing swords fiercely in the chamber, sparks and wind, two former brothers-in-arms in a desperate duel
> Seran attacks Veyr. The two deputies clash, their disagreement turning into a fight neither imagined they would have.
@fx KRANG | block
> Seran eventually gains the advantage and prepares to kill Veyr.
@panel splash | veyr, seran | Black energy erupting from the Centroid and flooding the chamber; a supernatural stone tomb rising around Veyr and dragging him beneath the cracking floor while Seran reaches in vain
> Suddenly, the Centroid resonates. Black energy floods the chamber.
THE VOICE: He is not yours to destroy.
> A supernatural stone tomb forms around Veyr and swallows him beneath the ground.
@fx GRRRMMM | stone
> Seran tries to break it, but the structure disappears before he can reach Veyr.

@page
@panel wide | thane | Several hooded figures in dark cloaks running away down a torch-lit stone corridor, seen from behind; at the back of the group Thane, unhooded, glances back over his shoulder
> The seven traitors flee.
> Kael looks toward the escaping fighters. He sees his older brother Thane among them.
@show left kael
KAEL [shocked]: Thane!
@panel wide | kael, thane | The two brothers facing each other in a torch-lit stone corridor: younger Kael anguished and furious on the left, his older brother Thane on the right turning back, conflicted
> Thane turns.
@show right thane
THANE: Come with us, Kael.
KAEL [angry]: You watched him kill Auren!
THANE: You don't understand what's coming.
KAEL: Then explain it!
@panel tall | thane | Thane turning away into the shadows of the corridor, his face hidden, leaving
> Thane cannot answer. He leaves.
@hide right

@page
@panel wide | auren, kael | The white-bearded Auren lying on his back on the stone floor, gravely wounded; young Kael kneeling beside him, holding his hand with both of his, the stone's glow fading behind them
> Kael kneels beside Auren. The dying founder struggles to speak.
@show right auren
AUREN: Kael...
KAEL: Don't move. Seran will help you.
AUREN: Listen to him.
KAEL [sad]: Please...
@panel square | auren | Close-up of the dying Auren lying on the stone floor, his head resting on the stones, a faint peaceful smile, looking up
AUREN: Don't let what happened here become everything you are.
@hide right
@panel strip | kael | Kael kneeling with his head bowed on the dark stone floor, tears falling, holding with both hands a pale, still, wrinkled old hand in a white-and-gold robe sleeve that lies on the floor in the foreground (only the hand and sleeve visible), the chamber silent and dark
> Auren dies.
> Kael remains holding his hand.
@hide all

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- P06
@card MONTHS LATER | Headquarters | The second betrayal
@bg hq_night

@page
@panel wide | seran | Seran, now commander, leading the training of loyal young fighters in the fortress courtyard at night, stern and determined
> Seran has become the leader of the seven loyal fighters.
> He learns that the traitors have received new powers from space and are preparing to steal the Centroid to release Veyr.
> The loyal fighters train under him.
@bg hq_siege
@panel splash | - | The mountain fortress under siege at night: walls exploding in black flames, lightning, swirling mist and flying rocks, shadowy figures with supernatural powers attacking
